WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.410
Classical commentators
tell of a case in Madinah.

2
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:07.330
A Muslim stole, then blamed
an innocent Jewish man.

3
00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:09.710
They link it to verses of the Qur'an.

4
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.210
The verses cleared the innocent man.

5
00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:17.120
Later in the same surah comes a standard
that reaches right into Muslim homes.

6
00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:20.770
What does that mean for Shari'ah,
the path Muslims follow?

7
00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.800
In this mission, you'll
read from Surah An-Nisa,

8
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:26.820
and see justice in the Prophet's own life.

9
00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.290
Then you'll explore where
Shari'ah comes from,

10
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:33.290
and how Muslims apply it
today, from food to banking.

11
00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.800
Your mission: find out how this
idea of justice shapes Shari'ah.
